{"step_index":336,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-24T09:39:31Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\nImplement advanced Stockfish analysis features.\n\n1. Add a vertical evaluation bar beside the chessboard.\n2. Display the evaluation score in centipawns.\n3. Display mate scores when Stockfish detects a forced mate.\n4. Show the best move suggested by Stockfish.\n5. Add an optional Best Move Analysis panel.\n6. Allow users to analyze the current position.\n7. Display the principal variation (PV) when available.\n8. Use real Stockfish UCI analysis output.\n9. Correctly convert centipawn scores according to the player's perspective.\n10. Make analysis asynchronous using the Web Worker.\n\nIMPORTANT:\nDo not generate fake evaluation scores or pretend to provide analysis when the engine has not returned results.\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-11-24T14:39:31+05:00.\n\nThe user's current state is as follows:\nActive Document: user is viewing tab agent-tab-1 (http://localhost:5173/, \"Stockfish Chess Arena | Grandmaster Engine\") (LANGUAGE_UNSPECIFIED)\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
{"step_index":337,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-24T09:40:48Z","model":"gemini-3.8-flash-high","input_tokens":3203,"cache_read_tokens":170834,"output_tokens":2007,"thinking":"I'm thinking through how to approach this.\n\n\nThe evaluation bar will be positioned vertically alongside the chessboard, indicating White and Black advantage based on the centipawn score, with the bottom of the bar matching the bottom player's color according to the `boardOrientation`. A sigmoid function will convert centipawn scores into a winning probability percentage for the bar's height, clamped between 5% and 95%, or 0% to 100% on mate. This will respect the standard chess.com convention.\n\n\nIf a mate is detected for White, the bar will be 100% White; for Black, 0% White (100% Black). The evaluation score will be displayed on the bar, including centipawn values, checkmates (M3, -M2), and smooth transitions between updates. The centipawn score from Stockfish needs conversion; the UCI protocol reports the score from the side to move's perspective. The absolute White score is determined by considering the turn, and both the absolute score and who is winning will be displayed.\n\n\nThe system needs to render the best move provided by the engine in both UCI and standard algebraic notation. This best move should also be highlighted on the board in analysis mode. An optional panel will provide detailed analysis, including the evaluation, depth, principal variation, and search statistics. The system will allow users to analyze the current position using the engine, with automatic restarting upon move updates.\n\n\nThe AI's move search will update the evaluation bar when it's the AI's turn; the engine evaluates and updates the bar in real time for human turns and analysis mode. Principal variation (PV) sequences from the engine will be displayed by converting the UCI move list into a numbered SAN sequence using a temporary simulator. Analysis will use real UCI output, displaying \"Evaluating...\" or \"Calculating...\" when scores are unavailable; centipawn scores will be correctly converted to reflect the player's perspective, clearly displaying the absolute score, advantage side, and mate status. Asynchronous analysis will be handled using the Web Worker.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"update_focus","args":{"focus":"Reviewing current Stockfish UCI adapter and service for analysis support"}},{"name":"read_file","args":{"EndLine":100,"Path":"C:\\Users\\DELL\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\stockfish-chess-arena\\src\\engine\\uciAdapter.ts","StartLine":1}}]}
