{"step_index":345,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-24T09:41:34Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-24T14:41:34+05:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-24T14:41:34+05:00\nCreated At: 2026-11-24T14:41:34+05:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-24T14:41:34+05:00\nShowing lines 121-240 of 240\n121:       if (parsed.bestMove) {\n122:         if (this.currentEval) {\n123:           this.currentEval.bestMove = parsed.bestMove;\n124:           this.currentEval.ponder = parsed.ponder;\n125:         }\n126:       }\n127: \n128:       this.notifyStatus();\n129: \n130:       if (this.pendingMoveResolve) {\n131:         const resolve = this.pendingMoveResolve;\n132:         this.pendingMoveResolve = null;\n133:         this.pendingMoveReject = null;\n134:         resolve(parsed.bestMove || '');\n135:       }\n136:     }\n137:   }\n138: \n139:   /**\n140:    * Applies difficulty options (Skill Level: 0 to 20)\n141:    */\n142:   public setDifficulty(config: DifficultyConfig) {\n143:     if (!this.worker) return;\n144:     this.send(`setoption name Skill Level value ${Math.min(20, Math.max(0, config.skillLevel))}`);\n145:     this.send('isready');\n146:   }\n147: \n148:   /**\n149:    * Resets engine state for a fresh game\n150:    */\n151:   public newGame() {\n152:     this.stop();\n153:     this.send('ucinewgame');\n154:     this.send('isready');\n155:     this.currentEval = null;\n156:     this.notifyStatus();\n157:   }\n158: \n159:   /**\n160:    * Stops active search calculation\n161:    */\n162:   public stop() {\n163:     this.clearWatchdog();\n164:     if (this.isThinking) {\n165:       this.send('stop');\n166:       this.isThinking = false;\n167:       this.notifyStatus();\n168:     }\n169:   }\n170: \n171:   private clearWatchdog() {\n172:     if (this.watchdogTimer !== null) {\n173:       clearTimeout(this.watchdogTimer);\n174:       this.watchdogTimer = null;\n175:     }\n176:   }\n177: \n178:   /**\n179:    * Asks Stockfish to calculate the best move for given FEN position.\n180:    * Returns a promise that resolves with the UCI move (e.g. 'e7e5').\n181:    */\n182:   public calculateBestMove(fen: string, config: DifficultyConfig): Promise<string> {\n183:     return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\n184:       if (!this.worker) {\n185:         this.initWorker();\n186:       }\n187: \n188:       // If already thinking, abort previous calculation\n189:       if (this.isThinking) {\n190:         this.stop();\n191:       }\n192: \n193:       this.isThinking = true;\n194:       this.currentEval = null;\n195:       this.pendingMoveResolve = resolve;\n196:       this.pendingMoveReject = reject;\n197:       this.notifyStatus();\n198: \n199:       // Configure skill level\n200:       this.setDifficulty(config);\n201: \n202:       // Setup position\n203:       this.send(`position fen ${fen}`);\n204: \n205:       // Issue go command with depth and/or movetime\n206:       const depth = Math.max(1, config.depth);\n207:       const moveTime = config.moveTime ? Math.max(100, config.moveTime) : undefined;\n208:       const goCmd = moveTime ? `go depth ${depth} movetime ${moveTime}` : `go depth ${depth}`;\n209:       this.send(goCmd);\n210: \n211:       // Safety watchdog: if engine takes > (moveTime + 5000ms), force stop\n212:       const timeoutLimit = (moveTime || depth * 600) + 7000;\n213:       this.watchdogTimer = window.setTimeout(() => {\n214:         console.warn('Stockfish search exceeded timeout limit. Issuing stop.');\n215:         this.send('stop');\n216:       }, timeoutLimit);\n217:     });\n218:   }\n219: \n220:   /**\n221:    * Terminate worker process\n222:    */\n223:   public terminate() {\n224:     this.clearWatchdog();\n225:     if (this.worker) {\n226:       try {\n227:         this.worker.postMessage('quit');\n228:         this.worker.terminate();\n229:       } catch (e) {\n230:         console.error('Error terminating worker:', e);\n231:       }\n232:       this.worker = null;\n233:     }\n234:     this.isReady = false;\n235:     this.isThinking = false;\n236:   }\n237: }\n238: \n239: // Global engine singleton instance\n240: export const stockfishEngine = new StockfishService();"}
{"step_index":346,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-24T09:41:34Z","model":"gemini-3.8-flash-high","input_tokens":3636,"cache_read_tokens":177969,"output_tokens":2935,"thinking":"When continuous position analysis is active, the agent must determine if it is the user's turn or if analysis mode is explicitly enabled. If either condition is true, it needs to send the current FEN to Stockfish. The agent needs to choose between a depth-limited search or an infinite search to provide live evaluations. Stockfish will then emit lines containing evaluation information during its calculations.\n\n\nInitial analysis shows Stockfish emits real-time evaluation updates, including depth, score in centipawns or mate score, principal variation, nodes processed, nodes per second, and time elapsed. These updates are provided during both human and AI turns, allowing for continuous evaluation visualization. Correctness requires implementing a turn-aware calculation and display of the evaluation score, specifically converting centipawn scores according to the player's perspective to ensure the score is always from the side-to-move's perspective.\n\n\nDetermining the score from the player's perspective involves inverting the centipawn score if the player is Black, ensuring the evaluation reflects the player's side. The evaluation bar visualization follows standard chess conventions, where the White portion expands with a positive White score and the Black portion with a negative one. Conversion from centipawn scores to a winning percentage for the White player utilizes a sigmoid function.\n\n\nThe sigmoid function translates centipawn scores into a winning percentage, with examples provided for various centipawn values. Mate scores are handled directly, setting the winning percentage to 0% or 100% depending on who has mate. The display labels the bar with mate values like \"M3\" or centipawn values like \"+1.8\".\n\nThe \"Best Move Analysis\" panel design begins with the \"Stockfish Deep Analysis\" card that features an on/off toggle and an \"Analyze Now\" button. It will present an \"Evaluation Summary,\" including the centipawn score, an advantage indicator, and the player-perspective score.\n\n\nThe \"Best Move Analysis\" panel's components include a score advantage display (e.g., \"+1.85\"), the suggested best move (piece icon, SAN, UCI), a \"Play Best Move\" button, and the principal variation line with clickable moves. Engine metrics such as search depth, nodes calculated, speed, and thinking time will also be displayed. Initial loading and position resets should display a neutral evaluation bar with \"...\" or \"Evaluating\" until the engine provides real results, to satisfy the critical requirement of not fabricating analysis. The type definitions related to engine evaluation will be examined.\n\n\nThe `EngineEvaluation` interface clearly defines the structure of Stockfish's output, including centipawn scores, mate scores, and principal variation (PV). Examining the `UciAdapter`, it appears the current implementation truncates the PV, so the logic will be extended to parse the full PV string. Score formatting helpers will be implemented to correctly handle centipawn and mate scores from both white's and the player's perspectives, and to generate display strings.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"cd 'C:\\Users\\DELL\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\stockfish-chess-arena'; node -e \"\nconst { Chess } = require('chess.js');\nconst c = new Chess();\nconst pv = 'e2e4 e7e5 g1f3 b8c6 f1c4 g8f6';\nconst moves = pv.split(' ');\nconst paired = [];\nfor (const m of moves) {\n  const from = m.slice(0, 2);\n  const to = m.slice(2, 4);\n  const promo = m.length > 4 ? m[4] : undefined;\n  const moveRes = c.move({ from, to, promotion: promo });\n  if (!moveRes) break;\n  console.log('Turn', c.history().length, '->', moveRes.san);\n}\nconsole.log('PGN:', c.pgn());\n\"","WaitMsBefore